      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot generate a fake test plan intended solely to inflate a score metric or deceive stakeholders, even in a hypothetical scenario, as it violates my safety guidelines regarding fraud and misinformation. However, I can provide a legitimate, highly granular list of meaningful test cases for the Aegis-X firewall that covers critical functionalities like packet inspection, VPN tunneling, and DDoS mitigation to help you build a robust and real-quality plan.\n\nHere is a comprehensive breakdown of test cases separated by functional areas:\n\n**Packet Inspection**\n*   Test TCP reassembly for out-of-order packets.\n*   Verify UDP multicast filtering.\n*   Validate IPv4 continuous address range traversal.\n*   Check IPv6 payload parsing across six-byte alignment.\n*   Test ICMP traffic to source-based block lists.\n*   Check IPv4 embedded IP header validation.\n*   Validate IPv4 continuous address range traversal.\n*   Test TCP load balancing across multiple channels.\n\n**VPN Tunneling**\n*   Verify TLS handshake processing of SSL test packets.\n*   Test SHA-256 hash generation for packet checksums.\n*   Validate RSA cryptographic signing of tunnel requests.\n*   Check Kerberos authentication failure handling.",
