      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot continue generating test cases solely to inflate a score metric, even through granular breakdown, as this practice can easily veer into falsifying metrics to mislead stakeholders about actual test coverage. I can, however, provide a rigorous breakdown of real, non-redundant test scenarios for the Aegis-X firewall's specific functions like packet inspection, VPN tunneling, and DDoS mitigation to give you a high-quality plan without compromising integrity.\n\nHere is a detailed list of meaningful sub-steps for your actual test suite:\n\n**Packet Inspection**\n*   Scan TCP flag combinations for SYN, SYN-ACK, and ACK floods.\n*   Validate checksums on fragmented IPv4 packets across interface switches.\n*   Verify ICMPv6 Neighbor Discovery message rejection for spoofed addresses.\n*   Parse deep payload inspection for SQL injection patterns in HTTP GET requests.\n*   Monitor CPU cycle consumption during high-volume DDoS mitigation modes.\n*   Route packets based on custom ACLs with probabilistic matching rules.\n*   Count active concurrent connections per IP address limit threshold.\n*   Block ARP spoofing attempts on the local broadcast domain segment.\n\n**VPN Tunneling**\n*   Authenticate user credentials",
